94139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416666 1080 "$(3,0)$ and $(2,-1)$" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416666 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416666 1083 #uuid "e6c04fe0-8935-5aff-a0db-580177fae6a8" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416659 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416660 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416661 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416664 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416665 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416667 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416667 1077 "selection" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416667 1078 #edb/ref 17592186416659 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416667 1079 #uuid "1b03f791-a25e-5d56-8bc4-3d32145b2ec9" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416668 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416657 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416668 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416658 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416668 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416662 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416668 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416663 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416668 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416666 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416668 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416668 1077 "selection" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416668 1078 #edb/ref 17592186416666 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416668 1079 #uuid "d47620cc-ff04-5478-975c-18645160652a" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416669 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416668 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416669 1069 "q-225139" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416669 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416669 1071 "![](images/33/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=2{v}^{2}+u,\\,y=u-{v}^{4}.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{3}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416669 1072 #uuid "aedbf0c6-276b-509d-933d-5c28129e8de2" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416669 1074 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{3}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{3},$ we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(2{v}^{2}+u,\\,u-{v}^{4}) \\\\  & =(2(1)^{2}+u,\\,u-{1}^{4}) \\\\  & =(2+u,\\,u-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{3}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=2+u,\\,y=u-1,\\,1\\ge u\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2+t,\\,y(t)=t-1,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(3,0)$ and $(2,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](images/2a/2ac0e0eac9e4633a8d29881782d8dfe93c4c594ca0f99912a98507822c97c4b4.png)" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416670 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416667 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416670 1069 "q-160633" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416670 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416670 1071 "![](images/5f/5f91cc8b30f9b764021cd84c374a328c7ffb1287a9f0dc6a211a3fadfac2fdbd.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y=uv.\n$$\n\nFind the image of $Δ$ under the action of $T.$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$*" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416670 1072 #uuid "b9cdc646-22ad-53d7-894a-78ecf8a59507" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416670 1074 "We're told that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$ So, to map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we transform each side of $Δ$ separately:\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{1},$ where we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,uv) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,u(0)) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,0), & 0\\le u\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a horizontal line segment traversed from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(1,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{2}.$ Here, we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,uv) &  \\\\  & =({1}^{2},\\,1v) &  \\\\  & =(1,\\,v), & 0\\le v\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a vertical line segment traversed from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{3}.$ Here, we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,uv) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,u(1)) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,u), & 1\\ge u\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a right-opening parabola traversed from the point $(1,1)$ to the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{4}.$ Here, we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,uv) &  \\\\  & =({0}^{2},\\,0v) &  \\\\  & =(0,\\,0), & 1\\ge v\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThis is the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nDrawing the images of the sides of our square, we obtain the following image of $Δ:$\n\n![](images/cf/cfcee7d6c19b748385a35291ab582e7ce0dace9a1207d014b64165caa6d3bc2a.png)" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416671 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416672 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416671 1062 #uuid "283e81ba-165c-5712-b058-a61afb12269f" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416671 1063 #edb/ref 17592186416670 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416672 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416674 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416672 1062 #uuid "526a1df8-1606-5e36-8deb-549a340f512b" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416672 1063 #edb/ref 17592186416669 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416673 1062 #uuid "ba6262b9-b0fe-5e23-a4c4-b3dd83e994ec" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416673 1063 #edb/ref 17592186290425 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416674 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416673 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416674 1062 #uuid "bc6691b7-166a-5089-867e-8ee8a5dc5783" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416674 1063 #edb/ref 17592186290422 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416675 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416671 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416675 1062 #uuid "c4aa2659-822f-5c81-9961-6d81d19483c6" 13194139534269 17592186045417 true] [17592186416675 1063 #edb/ref 17592186389063 13194139534269 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-23a36746-618b-5408-8fcd-c638b93c9f28" 17592186416656 "answer-31e82cf1-a965-5d27-8faf-45515b67a2ed" 17592186416657 "answer-3d9762f5-d942-5b02-90e1-433937835992" 17592186416658 "answer-59020315-291c-59c3-9224-961256ce3b94" 17592186416659 "answer-5cdefaa7-89d2-5114-a2e1-0fce719d5db3" 17592186416660 "answer-